WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Before sunrise, a woman sits on a cushion,

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.810
back upright, eyes half-closed.

3
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.740
For a long time, she barely moves.

4
00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:14.430
Her mind wanders to breakfast,
to work, to worries.

5
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.820
Each time, she notices,
and gently comes back.

6
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.420
Buddhists believe the Buddha reached
enlightenment through meditation,

7
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.740
seated under the Bodhi tree.

8
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.590
So what are Buddhists actually trying
to do with their minds when they sit so

9
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.970
still?

10
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:33.320
In this mission, you'll learn
the main methods Buddhists use,

11
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.450
and what each one is for.

12
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.560
Then you'll weigh up whether meditation
is the most important Buddhist practice

13
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:40.990
of all.

14
00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.380
Your mission: find out what Buddhists
are really trying to do with their minds

15
00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:46.520
when they meditate.
